Chapter: DeskLabelMetricsTest
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopFont
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopComposite
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `widget-label` and `widget-button` reserve `text-length * 8` logical pixels,
 an EIGHT PIXEL CELL hardcoded in `Widget.codex`, and the renderer then draws
 a proportional face. This prints the two numbers side by side so the gap is a
 table rather than an adjective.

 Measured 2026-08-21 with CMUNSS at 1600 wide, and it answers in BOTH
 directions: the four lowercase buttons reserve 49 to 72 device pixels MORE
 than they draw, and `CODEX` reserves 80 against 106 drawn, short by 26.
 Capitals are wider than the cell and lowercase is narrower, so the error is
 not a margin to be tuned but a per-string measurement that is missing.

 The under-reservation does no visible harm TODAY only because `flex-col-place`
 gives every child the container's full width, so the brand label is handed 320
 pixels rather than the 80 it asked for. That coupling is the finding: a width
 constraint that stops the full-bleed stretch will start clipping the labels
 the stretch is currently hiding. The cell has to be fixed FIRST.

 It walks the desk's OWN sidebar tree rather than a copy of its strings. A
 label listed here would measure this chapter; `desk-sidebar` measured here is
 the thing that ships.

 WHAT A GATED RUN PROVES IS NOT THE METRIC. `seed/Codex.img` carries no
 typeface and the battery attaches no disk, so the recorded answer is the
 no-volume line: it proves this chapter still compiles against `GopDesk` and
 `GopFont` and that the mount is reached, and NOTHING about type. The table
 with a face lives in `ShellRefinement.md` beside the command that rebuilds
 it, which needs an image from `build-boot-img.ps1` (L-NAMED, and the same
 shape as `desk-leading-metrics`).

Section: Body

  dlm-w : Integer = 1600

  label-of : WidgetNode -> Text
  label-of (n) = when n.wn-kind
    is WkLabel (t) -> t
    is WkButton (t) -> t
    is otherwise -> ""

  pad : Text, Integer -> Text
  pad (t) (n) = if text-length t >= n then t else pad (t & " ") n

  row : WidgetNode, GopFont, Integer -> Text
  row (n) (tf) (s) =
    let t = label-of n
    in let reserved = n.wn-min-w * s
    in let drawn = gfont-text-w tf t
    in pad (n.wn-id) 10 & pad ("chars " & integer-to-text (text-length t)) 10
       & pad ("reserved " & integer-to-text reserved) 15
       & pad ("drawn " & integer-to-text drawn) 12
       & "slack " & integer-to-text (reserved - drawn)

  walk : List WidgetNode, Integer, Integer, GopFont, Integer -> [Console] Integer
  walk (kids) (i) (n) (tf) (s) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else let k = list-at kids i
    in if text-length (label-of k) == 0 then walk kids (i + 1) n tf s
    else act
      r <- print-line-uni (row k tf s)
      walk kids (i + 1) n tf s
    end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing = act
    m <- gfat-mount-esp
    if m.gm-ok == False then print-line-uni "no FAT volume on the boot medium"
    else act
      let ppem = comp-glyph-h * ui-wscale dlm-w
      in let s = ui-wscale dlm-w
      in act
        f <- gfont-load (m.gm-vol) "CMUNSS.TTF" ppem
        if f.gf-ok == False then print-line-uni "CMUNSS.TTF: not loaded"
        else act
          let bar = widget-measure (desk-sidebar 0) (dk-theme-of 0 dk-adorn-default)
          in act
            print-line-uni ("sidebar pinned to     : " & integer-to-text (dk-sidebar-w * s))
            w <- walk (bar.wn-children) 0 (bar.wn-child-count) f s
            print-line-uni ("sidebar measured to   : " & integer-to-text (bar.wn-min-w * s))
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end

